{#- Shared helper for rendering an annotation's contents.

Model nodes declare a variable's type, units and frequency together, as
``Annotated[DataArray, "mm d-1", DAILY]``. All three matter to a reader of the
model pages, so the macro unwraps the ``Annotated[...]`` and renders what is
inside it, comma-separated. Anything else — a plain `int` setting, an input
with no declared units — renders whole.

Griffe hands a units string over quoted where the text does not parse as
Python (``'mm d-1'``) and as an ``ExprName`` where it does (``degC``), so string
elements get their quotes stripped and expression elements go through the stock
expression template, which keeps the cross-references.
-#}

{% macro contents(annotation) %}
  {%- if annotation is not none -%}
    {%- if annotation.left is defined and annotation.left|string == "Annotated" -%}
      {%- for element in annotation.slice.elements | default([], true) -%}
        {{- ", " if not loop.first -}}
        {%- if element is string -%}
          {{- element | trim("\"'") -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- with expression = element, backlink_type = "used-by" -%}
            {%- include "expression.html.jinja" with context -%}
          {%- endwith -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- with expression = annotation, backlink_type = "used-by" -%}
        {%- include "expression.html.jinja" with context -%}
      {%- endwith -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
